attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 35, `gmhB` to `dapD`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, 35 persistent and 1 shell, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 3% of calls {S1}. The model names 94 to 99.8% of them, fewest at column 35, `dapD`, 94% {S1}.

@variable **A single variable column breaks the first spine**: column 36, `yaeI`, shell, carried by 55%, the least plastic stretch of the window {S2.c36, P}. Then columns 37 to 51, `yaeH` to `fhuC`, are [[hydroxamate transport]] {S3, Q}. Columns 61 to 67, `yadN` to `yadC`, are [[fimbrial proteins]], carried by 27 to 57%, the stretch most in regions of plasticity, 37 to 85% {S6, P, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 96 against 63%, and hesitates less there, 0.14 against 0.59 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 63, `htrE`, a variable column, 1.05 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on a spine.** Columns 68 to 78, `panB` to `gcd`, are carried by 91 to 96%, all persistent {S7}. The last column is `cueO`, in 85% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 92% of genes**, 0.20 bits on average, perplexity 1.5 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.97 against 0.12 bits, and names fewer genes, 39% against 98% {C}.

